  "term": "Myers–Briggs Type Indicator",
  "definition": "The Myers–Briggs Type Indicator is a personality assessment tool, rooted in Jung’s psychology, that sorts people into paired trait preferences on four axes. In this source, those axes are extraversion–introversion, sensing–intuition, thinking–feeling, and judging–perceiving.",
